Fly a design many times with its inputs scattered at random, print how its apogee and landing spread, and export every flight

Usage: hpr mc [OPTIONS] <DESIGN>

Arguments:
  <DESIGN>
          The design: an OpenRocket .ork file, an HPR design (.hpr, or .hprz with its attachments), or a rocket's JSON (.json)

Options:
      --config <NAME>
          The motor configuration to fly: its number in the list the output shows, its name, or its id [default: the design's default, or its only one]

      --json
          Print one JSON document on standard output instead of text; errors too

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use color. Auto colors what goes to a terminal and heeds NO_COLOR, FORCE_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE. JSON output never has color
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --motor <NAME_OR_FILE>
          Fly this motor in place of the configuration's, lit at launch: a catalog designation or common name, or a .eng or .rse file

      --mount <NAME>
          The motor mount that --motor goes in, by its name or its component id [default: the configuration's, or the design's only one]

      --delay <S_OR_P>
          The ejection delay of --motor's motor: seconds from burnout to its charge (0 fires it at burnout), or P for a plugged motor [default: none, so it fires no charge]

      --latitude <DEG>
          The launch site's latitude, degrees north (south is negative)
          
          [default: 0]

      --longitude <DEG>
          The launch site's longitude, degrees east (west is negative)
          
          [default: 0]

      --elevation <M>
          The launch site's height above sea level, m
          
          [default: 0]

      --rail-length <M>
          The rail's length, m, from the rocket's aft end to the rail's top
          
          [default: 1.5]

      --inclination <DEG>
          The rail's angle above the horizon, degrees [default: 90, vertical]

      --heading <DEG>
          The direction the rail leans toward, degrees clockwise from true north [default: 0]

      --wind <M_S>
          A wind of this speed at every height, m/s [default: calm]

      --wind-from <DEG>
          The direction the wind blows from, degrees clockwise from true north
          
          [default: 0]

      --accept-design-errors
          Fly a design whose checks find errors, such as a motor wider than its mount

      --offline
          Take a motor the bundled catalog lacks from the cache of ThrustCurve.org only, never the network

      --runs <N>
          How many flights to fly, 1 to 100,000
          
          [default: 100]

      --seed <N>
          The run's seed: the same seed, design and options fly the same flights, bit for bit, on one platform
          
          [default: 0]

      --mass-sd <FRACTION>
          One standard deviation of each stage's mass without motors, as a fraction of it (0.02 is 2%)
          
          [default: 0]

      --cg-sd <M>
          One standard deviation of each stage's center of mass along the axis, m
          
          [default: 0]

      --drag-sd <FRACTION>
          One standard deviation of the rocket's zero-lift drag coefficient, as a fraction of it
          
          [default: 0]

      --impulse-sd <FRACTION>
          One standard deviation of each motor's total impulse, as a fraction of it; its propellant mass scales with it
          
          [default: 0]

      --burn-time-sd <FRACTION>
          One standard deviation of each motor's burn time, as a fraction of it, at the same impulse
          
          [default: 0]

      --delay-sd <S>
          One standard deviation of each motor's ejection delay, s
          
          [default: 0]

      --wind-sd <FRACTION>
          One standard deviation of the wind's speed at every height, as a fraction of it
          
          [default: 0]

      --wind-from-sd <DEG>
          One standard deviation of the wind's direction, degrees, about --wind-from
          
          [default: 0]

      --inclination-sd <DEG>
          One standard deviation of the rail's angle above the horizon, degrees
          
          [default: 0]

      --heading-sd <DEG>
          One standard deviation of the rail's heading, degrees
          
          [default: 0]

      --deployment-lag-sd <S>
          One standard deviation of each recovery device's lag after its trigger, s
          
          [default: 0]

      --export <FILE>
          Write every flight's draw and outcome to this .csv file, one row a flight, and a .meta.json sidecar beside it

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  Fly a design 200 times, its wind scattered, and see where it lands:
      hpr mc my-rocket.ork --runs 200 --wind 4 --wind-sd 0.25 --wind-from-sd 15
  Scatter the motor's impulse by 3% and save every flight:
      hpr mc my-rocket.ork --runs 1000 --impulse-sd 0.03 --export flights.csv

Guide: https://hpr.fusionspace.co/cli.html#hpr-mc
